+# Open Loops
+
+## LOOP-001 - Private fleet registration
+
+- Status: open; deferred under D-0001.
+- Gate: operator.
+- Success Condition: the private registration patch is applied and committed
+  with registry, decision, current-state and distribution-log updates together.
+
+The central agent prepared registry and distribution-log additions as a
+private patch outside this repository. No fleet membership is claimed here.
+The private console is the authoritative home for registration facts.
+Consult ignored `../local/HOST.md` for the patch location. Apply and verify
+that patch in a separately authorized private-console session after its
+existing work has been resolved.
+
+## LOOP-002 - Supported build verification
+
+- Status: open; blocked by absent supported toolchain.
+- Gate: operator.
+- Success Condition: a build using the documented MSVC toolchain completes,
+  with its command, compiler version and result recorded in WORK_LOG.md.
+
+MSVC and the Windows SDK are unavailable on this host. The existing Windhawk
+clang/MinGW syntax probe failed on audio GUID and interface definitions in
+its headers; it does not establish a failure under the documented MSVC
+toolchain. Obtain that toolchain and run root `build.ps1` as documented in
+`BUILD.md`, recording the result. Keep upstream source unchanged during this
+setup and do not start or install the application as part of verification.
+
+## LOOP-003 - Fresh native harness loading verification
+
+- Status: open; requires a fresh harness session.
+- Gate: operator.
+- Success Condition: a fresh harness session provides evidence that the root
+  bridge is automatically loaded with the expected instruction precedence.
+
+Manual reading of the bridge and Writ during installation does not prove
+automatic startup discovery. Start a fresh session with this repository as
+the working directory and inspect its actual loaded instructions according
+to `../local/rules/NATIVE_LOADING.md`. Record the harness version, relevant
+operator configuration, applicable instruction precedence, and loading
+evidence before closing this loop.
